<title>USA: USDA 7-State and U.S. Cattle on Feed.</title>
<headline>USDA 7-State and U.S. Cattle on Feed.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA U.S. cattle on feed. 7</p>
<p>states, 1,000-plus head feedlots (data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    7 MAJOR STATES --  Pct----1997-----1996     1995</p>
<p> On Feed March 1	 108   8,769    8,152    8,227</p>
<p>During February:</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 106   1,527    1,441    1,532</p>
<p> -Marketed		  99   1,529    1,541    1,372</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance   81	42	 52	 52</p>
<p> On Feed February 1    106   8,813-R  8,304    8,119</p>
<p>Note--On feed data include cattle placed on feed after beginning of quarter and marketed before the end of quarter.  </p>
<p>USDA cattle on feed in the United States (1,000-plus head</p>
<p>feedlots, data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    U.S. TOTAL --	Pct----1997-----1996</p>
<p> On Feed March 1	 106  10,275    9,696</p>
<p>During February:</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 103   1,772    1,713</p>
<p> -Marketed		  96   1,777    1,845</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance   85	61	 72</p>
<p> On Feed February 1    104  10,341-R  9,900</p>
<p>Note--On feed data include cattle placed on feed after</p>
<p>beginning of quarter and marketed before the end of quarter.</p>
<p>USDA revised Feb 1, 1997 cattle on feed to 8,813,000 head from 8,783,000 for the seven major states, and to 10,341,000 from 10,311,000 for the United States.</p>
<p>The seven major states are Arizona, California, Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Nebraska and Texas.</p>
</text>
